WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:07.420
Hi.&nbsp; I am B.L. Garrett. I’m a documentary
filmmaker. I make films on ordinary, average,

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:13.530
everyday people. Everybody’s got a story.
I got into filmmaking about three and a half

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:18.279
year’s ago. I wanted to make a film on my
88-year old grandfather.&nbsp; He grew up poor

00:00:18.279 --> 00:00:23.910
on a farm in Oklahoma. His father was a sharecropper.&nbsp;
He served in World War II and in the South

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:28.990
Pacific.&nbsp; Later he went on to start his own
business and have a successful career.&nbsp; He

00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:34.510
is really a modern-day John Wayne. I knew
nothing about filmmaking and really all my

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:40.460
resources came from YouTube which is kind
of a scary thought.&nbsp; There’s so much information

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:49.200
out there and I spent hundreds and hundreds
of hours researching cameras, lighting, audio,

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:57.760
tripods, monopods, shotgun mics, lavalier
mics, recorders. I mean you name it.&nbsp; So

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:03.769
today I’m gonna talk about the equipment
that I that I landed on and how it’s worked

00:01:03.769 --> 00:01:09.330
for me and the strengths and some of the weaknesses
of my equipment. The first thing I’ll talk

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:19.409
about is my camera. I landed on a Panasonic
gh3.&nbsp; At the time the gh2 was still out and

00:01:19.409 --> 00:01:26.330
kind of all the rage. You could go on Vimeo,
YouTube, I mean I would see this beautiful

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:35.840
footage of hacked gh2a and I was amazed by
really how small the camera was and that intrigued

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:43.679
me. I thought to get footage like that it
had to be this big, bulky camera that sat

00:01:43.679 --> 00:01:51.390
on your shoulder and I was just unaware that
a DSLR type camera could do something like

00:01:51.390 --> 00:01:59.819
that. I ended up going with the gh3 for a
couple of reasons. The main reason was battery

00:01:59.819 --> 00:02:09.490
life. I can literally on one battery use my
gh3 for almost five hours. Another thing that

00:02:09.490 --> 00:02:16.230
I like about my gh3 is that I can put a hundred
and twenty eight gig sd card in and film at

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:24.380
50 megabits per second for five and a half
hours, which is remarkable.&nbsp; So I always

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:30.010
have two hundred and twenty eight gig cards
on me.&nbsp; I have two batteries on me so if

00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:36.730
I ever go out to a shoot, say I have a subject
I’m making a film on and I go out and I

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:41.500
have an eight hour day, I can film all day
with those two batteries and really one sd

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:49.650
card (to tell you the truth). I go to the
other sd card, but you know usually the one

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:56.370
sd card gets me through the day. Some of the
things I really like about the gh3 is that

00:02:56.370 --> 00:03:03.340
it will film in 60 frames-per-second, 30 frames-per-second,
and 24 frames-per-second. I usually use 24

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:10.450
frames-per-second. It builds up to 72 megabits-per-second,
but I usually use the 50 megabits-per-second

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:19.540
and 24 frames-per-second and it really gives
me the 1080p HD-quality that I’m looking

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:28.590
for. I also love the LCD screen in the back.&nbsp;
It flips out. It swivels, so whenever I’m

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:35.140
interviewing somebody and I’m sitting next
to the camera, I can pull the LCD screen out

00:03:35.140 --> 00:03:41.200
sideways and I can monitor the footage to
make sure that we’re still recording and

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:48.110
to make sure that we’re in focus. That’s
a huge thing.&nbsp; It’s got a HDMI output that

00:03:48.110 --> 00:03:55.890
I love and it’s also got real time audio
jack where I can plug headphones in and listen

00:03:55.890 --> 00:04:09.250
to the in-camera audio. Audio wise, I use
two zoom h1 recorders.&nbsp; I use two lavalier

00:04:09.250 --> 00:04:16.150
mics that are made by Giant Squid.&nbsp; This
is really a great bargain.&nbsp; If you’re just

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:22.150
getting into filmmaking, there’s a lot of
recorders out there that I’m sure are much

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:26.630
better quality. But if you’re just getting
into filmmaking and you want to step up your

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:36.531
game to have something better than your in-camera
audio, I highly recommend the zoom H1.&nbsp; They

00:04:36.531 --> 00:04:46.561
cost $99 a piece and the Giant Squid lavalier
mics cost $50.&nbsp; So basically two audio recorders

00:04:46.561 --> 00:04:54.220
and two lavalier mics for $300 is a great
bargain. I also have a Rode video mic pro

00:04:54.220 --> 00:05:00.950
shotgun mic that I mount on the hot shoe on
top of the gh3 camera. I use that really to

00:05:00.950 --> 00:05:08.450
sink the audio with the recorded sound that
I get from the recorders and the lavalier

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:15.530
mic. I also use it for B-roll footage for
background noise and kind of chatter.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.530 --> 00:05:22.870
It works out great the gh3 is great because
the Micro Four Thirds cameras.&nbsp; It looks

00:05:22.870 --> 00:05:28.960
like a still camera, like just a regular picture
camera and it’s really great when I’m

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:33.550
out in public.&nbsp; I’m getting B-roll footage.&nbsp;
People think that I’m taking pictures. They

00:05:33.550 --> 00:05:39.390
don’t know that I’m getting the footage
from this little powerhouse.

00:05:39.390 --> 00:05:44.820
A lot of times friends and family that have
seen a lot of my stuff, I’ll be out and

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:50.580
I’ll have my camera and they’ll be like
“what camera do you use when you make your

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:56.660
films?” And I’m like “This camera right
here and it’s really amazing, the footage

00:05:56.660 --> 00:06:02.971
I get from it. It doesn’t shoot 4K, but
I don’t really need 4K yet, you know. I

00:06:02.971 --> 00:06:09.210
am looking to upgrade in the next six months
or so.&nbsp; I might go to the Panasonic gh4.

00:06:09.210 --> 00:06:16.870
I can tell you right now I looked on B&amp;H Photo
and you can buy a brand new gh3 for $549 and

00:06:16.870 --> 00:06:23.360
I’m seriously considering going that way.&nbsp;
I always, always, always – when I have a

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:31.010
job, I always ran an additional camera.&nbsp;
Usually the Panasonic gh3 I use LensRental.com.&nbsp;

00:06:31.010 --> 00:06:39.260
They’ve done me right.&nbsp; I’ve used them
probably two dozen times. They always ship

00:06:39.260 --> 00:06:46.470
it on time.&nbsp; It’s my same camera.&nbsp; I have
the lenses for it.&nbsp; I always have that for

00:06:46.470 --> 00:06:52.901
a backup and I’ve used one for a wide angle
shot and a close-up shot for my films.&nbsp; So

00:06:52.901 --> 00:06:59.220
if one fails me,&nbsp; I’ve got the backup.
Let’s talk about lenses.&nbsp; When I first

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:06.669
got the camera, something that I had learned
from the DrewNetwork, he talked about these

00:07:06.669 --> 00:07:16.169
iconic lenses that were made in the eighties
by Nikkor.&nbsp; So I bought a 28 mm, f/2.8 AIS

00:07:16.169 --> 00:07:23.540
and I bought a Nikkor 50 mm f/1.8.&nbsp;&nbsp; These
lenses were made in the early eighties and

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:28.780
it’s some of the some of the greatest glass
I’ve ever seen.&nbsp; Cool thing about it is

00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:38.430
I buy all my lenses used at&nbsp; Keh.com and
these things we’re not that expensive. I

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:45.169
think for the two lenses I spent almost $300.&nbsp;
So those were my first two lenses. I also

00:07:45.169 --> 00:07:53.520
purchased a 14 mm Panasonic pancake lens.
I believe it’s a f/2.5.&nbsp; So that was my

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:59.580
wide angle and it had autofocus, which is
nice when you’re shooting B roll and you’re

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:05.940
following somebody trying to do some Steadicam
work with your wide angle. It was really a

00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:15.650
nice piece to my collection.&nbsp; But all my
early films, I used the 50 mm and the 28 mm

00:08:15.650 --> 00:08:21.150
to interview my subjects and all my filming
was pretty much done with that. I’ve added

00:08:21.150 --> 00:08:29.030
two more lenses to my collection since then.
Last year I purchased an Olympus 45mm and

00:08:29.030 --> 00:08:37.999
it’s an F 1.8 and it is a beautiful portrait
lens for taking pictures and for filming.

00:08:37.999 --> 00:08:44.689
This is one of my favorite lenses and I bought
it I think for $250 brand new on Amazon.&nbsp;

00:08:44.689 --> 00:08:49.759
I think it was an international version and
you didn’t get a warranty with it but…

00:08:49.759 --> 00:08:56.160
you know I’ll roll the dice on that to save
a hundred bucks. Secondly my last lens and

00:08:56.160 --> 00:09:02.640
my most favorite lens is the Panasonic 12
to 35mm. That’s what I’m filming myself

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:16.750
on right now with my Panasonic gh3.&nbsp; It’s
got auto focus and it’s got on-board stabilization.

00:09:16.750 --> 00:09:22.129
Griffin Hammond made a documentary called
Sriracha and he made the whole documentary

00:09:22.129 --> 00:09:30.649
with my Panasonic gh3 and a Panasonic 12 to
35mm. I was blown away with the clarity, how

00:09:30.649 --> 00:09:37.130
it looked and I wanted to have one at the
time, it was like $1,200.&nbsp; I couldn’t afford

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:44.369
that so I waited a year and a half and I just
bought one without the warranty on Amazon

00:09:44.369 --> 00:09:51.970
for $765. It’s been a great addition.&nbsp;
It’s nice when I interview somebody…I

00:09:51.970 --> 00:09:59.819
mean the worst thing ever is interviewing
somebody for an hour and a half and then going

00:09:59.819 --> 00:10:07.709
home to edit and you pull up the footage and
it’s soft. It’s just soft enough where

00:10:07.709 --> 00:10:13.740
you’re like “I just can’t use this footage.”
It looked great when I focused in on him,

00:10:13.740 --> 00:10:20.600
but it was soft.&nbsp; So with the new lens, I
don’t have to worry about that with a 45mm

00:10:20.600 --> 00:10:29.589
or the 12 to 35mm.&nbsp; The Panasonic gh3 has
a two-time crop factor so my 45mm really is

00:10:29.589 --> 00:10:39.980
a 90mm and the 12-35 comes out to 24 to 70mm
focal length. Price was really a major factor

00:10:39.980 --> 00:10:50.870
in purchasing the used Panasonic gh3 from
Keh.com. I believe I bought it for $800 used.&nbsp;

00:10:50.870 --> 00:11:00.690
One thing about Keh.com is that how they market
the condition of the equipment is like no

00:11:00.690 --> 00:11:08.810
other.&nbsp; If it says “like new” I mean
it is brand new. It can say “excellent”

00:11:08.810 --> 00:11:13.429
all the way down to “bargain.”&nbsp; I have
friends who have bought bargain lenses and

00:11:13.429 --> 00:11:16.889
there was nothing wrong with them (they were
great).&nbsp; One thing I want to mention today

00:11:16.889 --> 00:11:20.410
about the company’s I’m talking about
that I’ve done business with, in no way

00:11:20.410 --> 00:11:25.779
am I paid by these companies. I’m just a
satisfied customer and believe me, you can

00:11:25.779 --> 00:11:30.449
check my bank account (it’s not that big).
Thank you guys SO much for watching.&nbsp; If

00:11:30.449 --> 00:11:34.920
you ever have any questions, you can contact
me directly at BL@BLGarrettFilms.com. Have

00:11:34.920 --> 00:11:36.719
a great day!

